# Theming — Material 3 / Stitch

## Active Theme

`StitchM3Theme` (`lib/theme/stitch_m3_theme.dart`) is the **canonical** theme.  
`AppTheme` in `lib/core/theme/app_theme.dart` is a secondary design-token layer — prefer `StitchM3Theme` for new work.

The app defaults to **dark mode** (`ThemeMode.dark`).

## Color Usage

Always resolve colors from the active `ColorScheme` — never hardcode hex values.

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
final cs = Theme.of(context).colorScheme;
Container(color: cs.surface);
Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(color: cs.onSurface));

// ❌ BAD
Container(color: const Color(0xFF121212));
```

Brand primary blue is `#0D59F2` — it is exposed as `colorScheme.primary` in `StitchM3Theme`.

## Typography

Use `Theme.of(context).textTheme` tokens (`headlineMedium`, `bodyLarge`, etc.).  
Do not set `fontSize` or `fontWeight` directly unless a precise one-off is needed and well documented.

## Spacing & Radius

Stitch spacing scale (8 px grid): 4 · 8 · 12 · 16 · 24 · 32 · 48.  
Use `BorderRadius.circular(12)` for cards/chips; `BorderRadius.circular(8)` for buttons (matches M3 defaults in theme).

## Responsive Layout

Use `lib/core/ui/breakpoints.dart` for adaptive layouts:

```dart
if (Breakpoints.isDesktop(context)) {
  // side-by-side layout
} else {
  // stacked layout
}
```

## Icons

Prefer `Icons.*` (Material) over `CupertinoIcons.*` to stay consistent with M3. Use `CupertinoIcons` only when explicitly targeting iOS affordances.
